### Anisotropic Noise

- Category: Texture generators > Noises
- Purpose: Generates grayscale noise of randomly colored strips that fade into one another.
- Main parameters: X amount, Y amount, Smoothness, Smoothness interpolation, Disorder, Non-square expansion.
- Nearest Copernicus node: none. No Copernicus node produces strip-based anisotropic noise (`Cop phasornoise` is wave-based, a different pattern).
- Mapping status: documented_only
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/texture-generators/noises/anisotropic-noise

